    "termsOfUse": "Researchers interested in the use of this dataset (\"Huizinga, Famke, 2025, \"Stimulation of Daily physical Activity (SoDA)\", https://doi.org/10.34894/MXV6PI, DataverseNL\") may send a request for access to the dataset.\nThe data may only be used for the purpose of conducting not-for-profit scientific research in the field of Oncology. It is not allowed to actively search online or any other way to re-identify persons involved in the dataset. It is not allowed to disclose the full version of the dataset to any third party or otherwise use it for your own benefit or for the benefit of a third party, without first obtaining written consent from the University of Groningen or University Medical Center Groningen.",
    "confidentialityDeclaration": "The signing of a Data Transfer Agreement may be part of the process of receiving permission to re-use the data for scientific research purposes.\n",
    "specialPermissions": "The Head of Department of \"Oncology in Primary Care\" or \"Primary and Long-term Care\" of the University Medical Center Groningen or, in their absence, the Ethics Board of the University Medical Center Groningen decide on the Request for Access.",
    "restrictions": "Access to the dataset is restricted because the relatively small geographical area participants originate from as well as specific data about their (visible) condition required for the original research, make the risk for re-identification and singling out too high to be more general available. This procedure respects the GDPR and the privacy statement of the University Medical Center Groningen (https://www.umcg.nl/privacy).",
    "termsOfAccess": "Permission for re-use can be granted by the University of Groningen Digital Competence Centre on behalf of the principle investigator after inspecting credentials and the reason for request. The procedure starts with a request for access via this dataset at DataverseNL. The Head of Department \"Oncology  in Primary Care\" or \"Primary and Long-term Care\" or, in their absence, the Ethics Board of the University Medical Center Groningen will assess the request. The signing of a Data Transfer Agreement may be part of the procedure for re-use of the data in research.",
    "fileAccessRequest": true,
